<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S5.T2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of features from different layers <math id="S5.T2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and fused features (<math id="S5.T2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\{2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\{2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>) in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ 3.3 Conditional Diffusion Representations ‣ 3 Diffusion Models Help Federated Learning ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.4 Denoising Diffusion Representations ‣ 3 Diffusion Models Help Federated Learning ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) to obtain <math id="S5.T2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.T2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="S5.T2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">best</span> in bold and <span id="S5.T2.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">second</span> with underline, <math id="S5.T2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">△</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle</annotation></semantics></math> means accuracy gap.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
