<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets:</span> We adopt popular benchmark datasets, including CIFAR10 &amp; CIFAR100 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, TinyImageNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>; we build unbalanced versions of these datasets by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>: CIFAR10-LT &amp; CIFAR100-LT, and TinyImageNet-LT; we use Digits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> and Office-Caltech <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> for the domain shift task in FL. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scenarios:</span> i) <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">label shift</span>: we consider two <em id="S5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">non-iid</em> settings: <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> follows Dirichlet distribution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>, where <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the heterogeneity level; <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a more extreme setting consists of 6 biased clients (each has only a single category) and 1 unbiased client has all categories.
ii) <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">imbalance shift</span>: we shape the original dataset into a long-tailed distribution with <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> means the ratio between sample sizes of the most frequent and least frequent class, as <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\max_{j}/\min_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\max_{j}/\min_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
iii) <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">domain shift</span>: Digits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> includes 4 domains as MNIST (M), USPS (U), SVHN (SV), SYN (SY) with 10 categories. Office-Caltech <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> also consists 4 domains as Caltech (C), Webcam (W), Amazon (A), DSLR (D) with 10 overlapping categories. We initialize 10 clients and assign them domains randomly: Digits (M: 1, U: 4, SV: 3, SY: 2), Office-Caltech (C: 3, W: 2, A: 2, D: 3). Each client’s dataset is randomly selected from domains (Digits: 10%, Office-Caltech: 20%). 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Configurations:</span> The global rounds <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> as 100 and clients <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> as 10, all methods have little or no gain with more rounds <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. To facilitate fair comparison, we follow in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, and use SGD optimizer to update models with a learning rate <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, a momentum of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, a batch size of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math>, the weight decay of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, and local epochs <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=10</annotation></semantics></math>. We use MobileNetV2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> for TinyImageNet, ResNet-10 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> for others. The dimension <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> as 512, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 4.1 Text-Driven Diffusion Contrasting ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>)) as 0.06, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.4 Denoising Diffusion Representations ‣ 3 Diffusion Models Help Federated Learning ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>)) as 150. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines</span>: We compare our against several SOTA methods: standard-based FedAvg <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>, FedProx <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>; contrast-based MOON <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, FedRCL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>; aggregate-based FedCDA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>, FedDisco <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>]</cite>; unsupervised FedEMA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib79" title="" class="ltx_ref">79</a>]</cite>, FedLID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>; prototype-based FedProto <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>, FedNH <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">72</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Validation Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We give ablation study in Table. <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>: i) TDCL brings significant performance improvements over the baseline, showing that TDCL is able to promote semantic spread-out property; ii) NDCR also yields solid gains, proving the importance of aligning instance embedding via consistency regularization; iii) combining TDCL and NDCR attain better performance, supporting our motivation to unleash meaningful guidance of diffusion representations to promote FL local training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we prove the advantage of fused features (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ 3.3 Conditional Diffusion Representations ‣ 3 Diffusion Models Help Federated Learning ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)). As shown in Table. <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, results on CIFAR10 reveal that fused features capture both semantics and local details, better than features on a single layer <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, and if the features with too low resolution (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>=1) or over-matching (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>=4) would damage the model’s performance. To explore the influence of different time-steps <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.4 Denoising Diffusion Representations ‣ 3 Diffusion Models Help Federated Learning ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>)), we conduct experiments on CIFAR10 with <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><mn>0.2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}</annotation></semantics></math> in Fig. <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> left, we add different amount of noise to get <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.4 Denoising Diffusion Representations ‣ 3 Diffusion Models Help Federated Learning ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). We find that <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> is robust to the choice of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[100,300]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>100,300</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[100,300]</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>=150 achieves the highest value). With the increase of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, more and more details are removed and semantic-level features are preserved, but when <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is too large, the object structure is distorted in the sample, making poor performance. In Fig. <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> right, we show the results with different <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 4.1 Text-Driven Diffusion Contrasting ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), which reveals that <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> is not sensitive to the <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[0.04,0.08]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.04</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[0.04,0.08]</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating the effectiveness of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ 4.1 Text-Driven Diffusion Contrasting ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>)), to balance relative distances among different samples. The accuracy no longer increases after <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>=0.06. Extra results of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> are provided in Appendix <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">C.2.5</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Evaluation Results</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The results on different settings (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>) in Table. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> consistently outperforms these counterparts, it confirms that <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> effectively leverages the inherent fine-grained visual representation capabilities of diffusion models to promote heterogeneous FL training. The results of Office-Caltech with domain shift are shown in Table. <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, indicating that <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> can acquire well-generalizable property in the feature space. With self-supervised scenario, in Table. <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, our <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> achieves excellent performance by leveraging the visual perception capability of diffusion models, without requiring any labeled data. The results with the imbalance shift on CIFAR100-LT and TinyImageNet-LT datasets, and the results with domain shift on the Digits, are given in Appendix <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">C.2.2</span> and <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">C.2.3</span>.
We also compare the convergence rate of <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> and baselines, shown in Appendix <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">C.2.4</span>, indicating the superiority of <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> in dealing with heterogeneous FL scenarios and the efficiency for FL model training.
The ablation study on the number of clients <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and local epochs <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> are provided in Appendix <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">C.2.7</span> and <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">C.2.8</span>.
Since our <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> is built on the SD model, we also investigate how the SD model’s weights would affect the performance of <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>. In our previous experiments, SD-1.5 as basic SD model, we then compare different versions (<span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, SD-1.4, SD-2.0) of the SD model on CIFAR10, and the results are shown in Appendix <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">C.2.9</span> (<span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, SD-1.4 get 83.09% and 88.23% of <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}_{0.05}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><mn>0.05</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}_{0.05}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><mn>0.2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}</annotation></semantics></math>). Our initial purpose is not to generate the image, different SD model versions have almost little difference.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To further elaborate on the core idea of <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>, <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, we study how to fully leverage the fine-grained visual representation capabilities from diffusion models (<span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, condense visual concepts and their relations) to boost the performance of heterogeneous FL, we set the following experiments: 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i) To ensure a fair comparison</span>, we also compare diffusion-based FL methods FedDISC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite> and FedDDA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">76</a>]</cite>, which build synthetic datasets to enhance performance. Moreover, we generate data for each client (same amount) by the SD model as <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diamondsuit" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">♢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diamondsuit</annotation></semantics></math>, and align SD features (the image is fed directly into the SD model) by L2 loss as <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math>. Table. <a href="#S5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows that directly matching SD features may even hurt the performance, which further illustrates the superiority of our <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ii) We focus on visual perception ability of diffusion models to understand an image (e.g., textures and structures) rather than pre-trained prior knowledge.</span> We conduct experiments on medical and remote sensing datasets HAM10000 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite> and EuroSAT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>, which are not crossed in SD pre-training dataset LAION-5B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>. Results of intra-domain (Table. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and cross-domain (Table. <a href="#S5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) datasets show that the success of <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> is based on the fine-grained visual representation rather than the large prior knowledge in SD model. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">iii) The SD model can implicitly provide both high-level and low-level visual concepts of semantic objects, while foundation models focus more on sparse visual matching.</span> Due to the natural heterogeneity in FL, simply aligning the features of foundation models may lead to local overfitting. We align FedAvg features with foundation model by L2 loss, shown in Table. <a href="#S5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, which show that <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> can capture underlying properties and correspondences of visual objects. Our TDCL and NDCR modules unlock the semantic-generative and fine-grained representation capabilities in the SD model to promote model training in heterogeneous FL.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we aim to exploit the fine-grained visual representation capabilities of diffusion models to handle data heterogeneity in FL.
We propose a novel diffusion-inspired FL framework <span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> to regulate local training via denoising and conditional diffusion representations.
By leveraging complementary strength of TDCL and NDCR, <span id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> achieves superior performance in heterogeneous FL.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Acknowledgment</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work is supported by the scholarship from the China Scholarship Council (CSC) while the first author pursues his PhD degree at the University of Wollongong. This work was also partially supported by Australian Research Council Linkage Project LP210300009 and LP230100083.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Algorithm Pseudocode Flow</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we describe the pseudocode of <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix A Algorithm Pseudocode Flow ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>: i) Client Process: for each client <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, loss as <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{TDCL}+\mathcal{L}_{NDCR}+\mathcal{L}_{CE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{TDCL}+\mathcal{L}_{NDCR}+\mathcal{L}_{CE}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">14</span>); ii) Server Process: aggregate all local models (same as FedAvg <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Pseudocode of <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>.</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          <em id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">/*  Global Server Process  */</em>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
          Initialized global rounds <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, number of clients <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, number of classes <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th client’s dataset <math id="alg1.l2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, client local model <math id="alg1.l2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and global model <math id="alg1.l2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
          Note: Conditional Diffusion Representations <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq.<span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">8</span>), Denoising Diffusion Representations <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq.<span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">9</span>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each round <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1,2,...,R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1,2,...,R</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{r}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{r}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> (server selects a random subset of <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> clients)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each client <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in A_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in A_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">in parallel</span> <span id="alg1.l6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}\leftarrow\text{RunClient}(w_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>RunClient</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}\leftarrow\text{RunClient}(w_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            <em id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// global aggregation</em>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{g}\leftarrow\sum_{k=1}^{|A_{r}|}\frac{n_{k}}{N}w_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{g}\leftarrow\sum_{k=1}^{|A_{r}|}\frac{n_{k}}{N}w_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
          <em id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">/*  Local Client Process  */</em>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
          Initialized local epochs <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, size of samples <math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="alg1.l13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, local model <math id="alg1.l13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, client’s dataset <math id="alg1.l13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each local epoch <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}=1,2,...,E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}=1,2,...,E</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each batch <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in</annotation></semantics></math> client dataset <math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{CE}=\sum_{i\in b}-\mathbf{1}_{y_{i}}\log(\psi(f(w_{k};x_{i})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{CE}=\sum_{i\in b}-\mathbf{1}_{y_{i}}\log(\psi(f(w_{k};x_{i})))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
            
            
             <em id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// Text-driven Diffusion Contrastive Learning</em>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{TDCL}\leftarrow\{z_{i},\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{i},\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{\mathcal{N}_{i}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{TDCL}\leftarrow\{z_{i},\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{i},\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{\mathcal{N}_{i}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq.<span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">11</span> in Sec.<span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">4.1</span>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
            
            
             <em id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// Noise-driven Diffusion Consistent Restriction</em>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{NDCR}\leftarrow\{z_{i},\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{NDCR}\leftarrow\{z_{i},\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq.<span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">12</span> in Sec.<span id="alg1.l20.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">4.2</span>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
            
            
             <em id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// training loss objective</em>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{CE}+\mathcal{L}_{TDCL}+\mathcal{L}_{NDCR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{CE}+\mathcal{L}_{TDCL}+\mathcal{L}_{NDCR}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
            
            
             <em id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// model update by the SGD optimizer</em>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{k}\leftarrow w_{k}-\eta\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k};b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}\leftarrow w_{k}-\eta\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k};b)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l25.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l26.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Analysis for <span id="A2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we herein provide insights into the convergence analysis for <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> under the non-convex case. This theoretical analysis of <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> is grounded in four standard assumptions prevalent in the field of FL, which are similarly invoked across various scholarly works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>. The detailed description of notations in Sec. <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Preliminaries ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, standard assumptions in Sec. <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, and our proofs in Sec. <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we introduce some additional variables to better represent the FL training process and model updates from a mathematical perspective. For the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th client, based on Sec. <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">3.1</span>, define the local model <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=g(h(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=g(h(x))</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is the feature extractor maps each sample <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to a <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dim feature vector <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=h(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=h(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is the classifier maps vector <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> into a <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}|</annotation></semantics></math>-dim output logits <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=g(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=g(z)</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{k}=\left\{x_{i},y_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{k}=\left\{x_{i},y_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the training dataset for the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th client, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of total samples, the label <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of single sample belongs to one of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}|</annotation></semantics></math> categories and is expressed as <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in\{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{C}|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in\{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{C}|\}</annotation></semantics></math>. In <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> process, for the client <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, given the sample pair <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{i},y_{i}\}\in\mathcal{D}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{i},y_{i}\}\in\mathcal{D}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, based on Sec. <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">3.3</span> and Sec. <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">3.4</span>, we can obtain conditional diffusion representations <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">8</span>), and denoising diffusion representations <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">9</span>). We denote the loss objective function <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{TDCL}(\text{Eq. {\color[rgb]{0.21,0.49,0.74}11}})+\mathcal{L}_{NDCR}(\text{Eq. {\color[rgb]{0.21,0.49,0.74}12}})+\mathcal{L}_{CE}(\text{Eq. {\color[rgb]{0.21,0.49,0.74}13}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Eq. </mtext><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;" mathcolor="#367DBD">11</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Eq. </mtext><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;" mathcolor="#367DBD">12</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Eq. </mtext><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;" mathcolor="#367DBD">13</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{TDCL}(\text{Eq. {\color[rgb]{0.21,0.49,0.74}11}})+\mathcal{L}_{NDCR}(\text{Eq. {\color[rgb]{0.21,0.49,0.74}12}})+\mathcal{L}_{CE}(\text{Eq. {\color[rgb]{0.21,0.49,0.74}13}})</annotation></semantics></math> defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with a subscript indicating the round <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> of the global iterations in our <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> process.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We express <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}\in\{1,2,\ldots,E\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}\in\{1,2,\ldots,E\}</annotation></semantics></math> as the local iteration step, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> as the global round, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> as the local epochs, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rE+\mathbf{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rE+\mathbf{e}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}</annotation></semantics></math>-th local update in round <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rE+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rE+1</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the time between <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-th global aggregation at the server and starting the model update on round <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+1</annotation></semantics></math> at the local client. Therefore, if the step is at <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rE+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rE+1</annotation></semantics></math> of local client iterations, the local model is the same as <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rE</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Assumptions</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k,r}(u_{k,r})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k,r}(u_{k,r})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the feature extractor, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{k,r}(v_{k,r})\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{C}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k,r}(v_{k,r})\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{C}|}</annotation></semantics></math> be the classifier to calculate logits, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k,r}=\{u_{k,r},v_{k,r}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k,r}=\{u_{k,r},v_{k,r}\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes parameters of the client model <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{k,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{k,r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{k,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{k,r}</annotation></semantics></math> means the objective function, at the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th client on the round <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. Our theoretical analysis of <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> is based on the following four standard assumptions in FL:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothness)<span id="Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each objective function <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz smooth,
which suggests the gradient of objective function <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuous:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{1}}-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{2}}\|_{2}\leq L_{1}\|w_{k,r_{1}}-w_{k,r_{2}}\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{1}}-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{2}}\|_{2}\leq L_{1}\|w_{k,r_{1}}-w_{k,r_{2}}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\;r_{1},r_{2}&gt;0,\kern 5.0ptk\in\{1,\ldots,K\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∀</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\;r_{1},r_{2}&gt;0,\kern 5.0ptk\in\{1,\ldots,K\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">since the smoothness depends on the derivative of the differentiable function,
it also indicates the following quadratic bound (<math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{1}}-\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{2}}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{1}}-\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{2}}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\nabla\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{2}})^{\top}(w_{k,r_{1}}-w_{k,r_{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\nabla\mathcal{L}_{k,r_{2}})^{\top}(w_{k,r_{1}}-w_{k,r_{2}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L_{1}}{2}\|w_{k,r_{1}}-w_{k,r_{2}}\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L_{1}}{2}\|w_{k,r_{1}}-w_{k,r_{2}}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unbiased Gradient and Bounded Variance)<span id="Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each client, the stochastic gradient is unbiased (<math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> is the sample of the client’s dataset),
so the unbiased gradient is expressed as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\zeta}[\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r},\zeta)]=\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r})=\nabla\mathcal{L}_{r}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\zeta}[\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r},\zeta)]=\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r})=\nabla\mathcal{L}_{r},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\;k\in\{1,\ldots,K\},\kern 5.0ptr&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\;k\in\{1,\ldots,K\},\kern 5.0ptr&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and has bounded variance:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\zeta}[\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r},\zeta)-\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r})\|_{2}^{2}]\leq\sigma^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\zeta}[\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r},\zeta)-\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r})\|_{2}^{2}]\leq\sigma^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E20Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\;k\in\{1,\ldots,K\},\kern 5.0pt\sigma^{2}\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\;k\in\{1,\ldots,K\},\kern 5.0pt\sigma^{2}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded Dissimilarity of Stochastic Gradients)<span id="Thmassumption3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each objective function <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>,
there exists constant <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> such that the stochastic gradient is bounded:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E21X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\zeta}[\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r},\zeta)\|_{2}]\leq B," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\zeta}[\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(w_{k,r},\zeta)\|_{2}]\leq B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E21Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\;k\in\{1,\ldots,K\},\kern 5.0ptB&gt;0,\kern 5.0ptr&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\;k\in\{1,\ldots,K\},\kern 5.0ptB&gt;0,\kern 5.0ptr&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 4</span></span><span id="Thmassumption4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Continuity)<span id="Thmassumption4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each real-valued function <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(u)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuous:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|h_{k,r_{1}}(u_{k,r_{1}})-h_{k,r_{2}}(u_{k,r_{2}})\|\leq L_{2}\|u_{k,r_{1}}-u_{k,r_{2}}\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|h_{k,r_{1}}(u_{k,r_{1}})-h_{k,r_{2}}(u_{k,r_{2}})\|\leq L_{2}\|u_{k,r_{1}}-u_{k,r_{2}}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E22Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\;r_{1},r_{2}&gt;0,\kern 5.0ptk\in\{1,\ldots,K\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∀</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\;r_{1},r_{2}&gt;0,\kern 5.0ptk\in\{1,\ldots,K\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Completing Proofs</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, based on the above four assumptions, we present the following three theorems and prove them:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Deviation bound of the objective function <math id="Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumptions, after every communication round, objective function <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> of an arbitrary client will be bounded,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E23X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\left(\eta-\frac{L_{1}\eta^{2}}{2}\right)EB^{2}+\frac{L_{1}E\eta^{2}}{2}\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\left(\eta-\frac{L_{1}\eta^{2}}{2}\right)EB^{2}+\frac{L_{1}E\eta^{2}}{2}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E23Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}|</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of classes, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{L_{1},L_{2},B,\sigma^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{L_{1},L_{2},B,\sigma^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are the constants in the above assumptions. Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Deviation bound of the objective function ℒ). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> indicates that <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> decreases as round <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> increases, and the convergence of our <span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> can be guaranteed by choosing an appropriate <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Non-convex convergence of <span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumptions, the objective function <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> of an arbitrary client decreases monotonically as the round increases with the following condition,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E24X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{\mathbf{e}}&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>𝐞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{\mathbf{e}}&lt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2B^{2}-2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}B}{L_{1}(\sigma^{2}+B^{2})},\;\mathbf{e}\in\{1,2,\ldots,E-1\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2B^{2}-2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}B}{L_{1}(\sigma^{2}+B^{2})},\;\mathbf{e}\in\{1,2,\ldots,E-1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Non-convex convergence rate of <span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the assumptions hold, the round <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R-1</annotation></semantics></math>, given any <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective function <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> will converge when,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R&gt;\frac{2(\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}^{*})}{\xi E\eta(2-L_{1}\eta)-\varOmega_{1}-\varOmega_{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R&gt;\frac{2(\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}^{*})}{\xi E\eta(2-L_{1}\eta)-\varOmega_{1}-\varOmega_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and we can further get the following condition for <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&lt;\frac{2\xi-2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}B}{L_{1}(\xi+\sigma^{2})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&lt;\frac{2\xi-2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}B}{L_{1}(\xi+\sigma^{2})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varOmega_{1}=2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varOmega_{1}=2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varOmega_{2}=L_{1}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varOmega_{2}=L_{1}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the optimal solution of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}=\min\{\mathcal{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}=\min\{\mathcal{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Deviation bound of the objective function ℒ). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> indicates the deviation bound of the objective function <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> for an arbitrary client after each round, and the convergence can be guaranteed by choosing appropriate <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Non-convex convergence of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is to ensure the expected deviation of <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> to be negative, so <span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>’s objective function converges, which can guide the choice of appropriate values for the learning rate <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> to guarantee the convergence.
Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Non-convex convergence rate of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> provides the convergence rate of <span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>: the smaller <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is, the larger <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is, which means that the tighter the bound is, the more communication rounds <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is required.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.1 </span>Completing the Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Deviation bound of the objective function ℒ). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Deviation bound of the objective function ℒ). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">The Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Deviation bound of the objective function ℒ). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is applicable to an arbitrary client in <span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>, therefore we omit the client’s notation <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the gradient descent as <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{r+1}=w_{r}-\eta\nabla\mathcal{L}_{r}(w_{r})=w_{r}-\eta\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{r+1}=w_{r}-\eta\nabla\mathcal{L}_{r}(w_{r})=w_{r}-\eta\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can get:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E27X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{rE+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{rE+2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}+(\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+1})^{\top}(w_{rE+2}-w_{rE+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}+(\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+1})^{\top}(w_{rE+2}-w_{rE+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E27Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L_{1}}{2}\|w_{rE+2}-w_{rE+1}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L_{1}}{2}\|w_{rE+2}-w_{rE+1}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E27Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}-\eta(\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+1})^{\top}\theta_{rE+1}+\frac{L_{1}}{2}\|\eta\theta_{rE+1}\|_{2}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}-\eta(\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+1})^{\top}\theta_{rE+1}+\frac{L_{1}}{2}\|\eta\theta_{rE+1}\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz quadratic bound of the above Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Smoothness). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
We perform the expectation on both sides:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
