</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> from the stochastic gradient is unbiased in Eq. <a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Assumption 2 (Unbiased Gradient and Bounded Variance). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> of the Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Unbiased Gradient and Bounded Variance). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>;
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> from the formula: <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{Variance}(x)=\mathbb{E}[x^{2}]-\mathbb{E}^{2}[x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Variance</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{Variance}(x)=\mathbb{E}[x^{2}]-\mathbb{E}^{2}[x]</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math> from the Eq. <a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Assumption 2 (Unbiased Gradient and Bounded Variance). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> of the Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Unbiased Gradient and Bounded Variance). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Then, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rE+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rE+1</annotation></semantics></math> means the time between the server and client, and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rE+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rE+2</annotation></semantics></math> means the first step,
we telescope <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> steps on both sides of the above equation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}+(\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2}-\eta)\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}+(\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2}-\eta)\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E29Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L_{1}}{2}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L_{1}}{2}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">and then we consider the relationship between <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{rE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{rE}</annotation></semantics></math>,
that is, given the any sample <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the relationship between <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E30X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}+(\mathcal{L}_{CE,(r+1)E+1}+\mathcal{L}_{TDCL,(r+1)E+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}+(\mathcal{L}_{CE,(r+1)E+1}+\mathcal{L}_{TDCL,(r+1)E+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="14" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E30Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathcal{L}_{NDCR,(r+1)E+1})-\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathcal{L}_{NDCR,(r+1)E+1})-\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E30Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}+\mathcal{L}_{TDCL,(r+1)E+1}-\mathcal{L}_{TDCL,(r+1)E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}+\mathcal{L}_{TDCL,(r+1)E+1}-\mathcal{L}_{TDCL,(r+1)E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E30Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}+\log(\sum_{\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j}\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{\mathcal{N}_{i},(r+1)E+1}}\text{exp}(s(\zeta,\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mtext>exp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}+\log(\sum_{\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j}\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{\mathcal{N}_{i},(r+1)E+1}}\text{exp}(s(\zeta,\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E30Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log(\sum_{\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j}\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{\mathcal{N}_{i},(r+1)E}}\text{exp}(s(\zeta,\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mtext>exp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log(\sum_{\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j}\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{\mathcal{N}_{i},(r+1)E}}\text{exp}(s(\zeta,\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
