<tr id="A2.E30Xm" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30Xm.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(vii)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(vii)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30Xm.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{n_{k}}{N}\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\theta_{k,rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{n_{k}}{N}\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\theta_{k,rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> from the objective function in Paper Eq. <span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">11</span>;
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> based on Paper Eq. <span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.9.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">10</span>: <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(z,\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j})=(\frac{1}{\mathcal{U}}\cdot\frac{1}{\|z\|_{2}}\cdot\frac{\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j}}{\|\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j}\|_{2}})z\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(z,\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j})=(\frac{1}{\mathcal{U}}\cdot\frac{1}{\|z\|_{2}}\cdot\frac{\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j}}{\|\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j}\|_{2}})z\leq z</annotation></semantics></math>, then we take expectation to get <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[s(z,\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j})]\leq\|z\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[s(z,\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{j})]\leq\|z\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=h(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=h(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math> from the formula as: <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|_{2}-\|y\|_{2}\leq\|x-y\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|_{2}-\|y\|_{2}\leq\|x-y\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iv)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iv)</annotation></semantics></math> details from the Sec. <span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.9.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">3.1</span> and Sec. <span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.9.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">3.3</span>, and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> is the sample of the client dataset;
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v)</annotation></semantics></math> from the Eq. <a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Assumption 4 (Continuity). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> of the Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Continuity). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>;
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(vi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(vi)</annotation></semantics></math> from the the fact that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is a subset of <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\{u,v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\{u,v\}</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(vii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(vii)</annotation></semantics></math> from the formula as <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\sum{x}\|_{2}\leq\sum{\|x\|_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\sum{x}\|_{2}\leq\sum{\|x\|_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we perform the expectation on both sides of Eq. <a href="#A2.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.1 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E+1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}\;+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}\;+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{n_{k}}{N}\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\theta_{k,rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{n_{k}}{N}\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\theta_{k,rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E31Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta EB," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta EB,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> from Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Bounded Dissimilarity of Stochastic Gradients). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, and we can easily get:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}]\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta EB," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{rE+1}]\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta EB,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text">then, based on Eq. <a href="#A2.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.1 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a> and Eq. <a href="#A2.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.1 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>, we can get:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E33X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta EB+\frac{L_{1}}{2}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta EB+\frac{L_{1}}{2}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E33Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2}-\eta)\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2}-\eta)\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E33Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{rE}-(\eta-\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2})EB^{2}+\frac{L_{1}E\eta^{2}}{2}\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{\leq}\mathcal{L}_{rE}-(\eta-\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2})EB^{2}+\frac{L_{1}E\eta^{2}}{2}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E33Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.12.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> from the Eq. <a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Assumption 3 (Bounded Dissimilarity of Stochastic Gradients). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> of the Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Bounded Dissimilarity of Stochastic Gradients). ‣ B.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Deviation bound of the objective function ℒ). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> indicates the deviation bound of the loss objective function for an arbitrary client after each communication round. Convergence can be guaranteed when there is a certain expected one-round decrease, which can be achieved by choosing an appropriate <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. We have completed the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Deviation bound of the objective function ℒ). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for <span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.2 </span>Completing the Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Non-convex convergence of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Non-convex convergence of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Based on Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Deviation bound of the objective function ℒ). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we can get:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E34X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]-\mathcal{L}_{rE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]-\mathcal{L}_{rE}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-(\eta-\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2})EB^{2}+\frac{L_{1}E\eta^{2}}{2}\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-(\eta-\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2})EB^{2}+\frac{L_{1}E\eta^{2}}{2}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E34Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, to ensure the right side of the above equation <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}=-(\eta-\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2})EB^{2}+\frac{L_{1}E\eta^{2}}{2}\sigma^{2}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}=-(\eta-\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2})EB^{2}+\frac{L_{1}E\eta^{2}}{2}\sigma^{2}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
we can easily get the following condition for <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E35X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{\mathbf{e}}&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>𝐞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{\mathbf{e}}&lt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E35X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2B^{2}-2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}B}{L_{1}(\sigma^{2}+B^{2})},\;\mathbf{e}\in\{1,2,\ldots,E-1\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2B^{2}-2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}B}{L_{1}(\sigma^{2}+B^{2})},\;\mathbf{e}\in\{1,2,\ldots,E-1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">So, the convergence of objective function <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> in <span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> holds as round <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> increases and the above limitation of the learning rate <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#A2.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.2 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>. We have completed the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Non-convex convergence of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for <span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.3 </span>Completing the Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Non-convex convergence rate of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Non-convex convergence rate of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Based on the Eq. <a href="#A2.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.1 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>, we can get:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E36X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B+\frac{L_{1}}{2}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{L}_{rE}+(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B+\frac{L_{1}}{2}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E36Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2}-\eta)\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(\frac{L_{1}}{2}\eta^{2}-\eta)\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Further, we can get the following equation by Eq. <a href="#A2.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.3 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E37X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}\;+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}\;+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E37Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2(\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}])+L_{1}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2(\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}])+L_{1}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Let the round <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R-1</annotation></semantics></math>, step <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, we can easily get the following equation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E38X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{RE}\sum_{r=0}^{R-1}\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{RE}\sum_{r=0}^{R-1}\sum_{\mathbf{e}=1}^{E-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{rE+\mathbf{e}}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\sum_{r=0}^{R-1}(\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}])}{RE(2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\sum_{r=0}^{R-1}(\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}])}{RE(2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E38Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta B}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta B}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E38Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L_{1}\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L_{1}\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">and then, given any <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> receive the limitation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E39X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\xi}&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\xi}&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\frac{2}{RE}\sum_{r=0}^{R-1}(\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}])}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}\;+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\frac{2}{RE}\sum_{r=0}^{R-1}(\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}])}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}\;+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E39Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta B+L_{1}\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}\eta B+L_{1}\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}}{2\eta-L_{1}\eta^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">then we can easily get the following condition for <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E40X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R&gt;\frac{2(\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}^{*})}{\underbrace{\xi E\eta(2-L_{1}\eta)-\varOmega_{1}-\varOmega_{2}}_{T_{2}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></munder></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R&gt;\frac{2(\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}^{*})}{\underbrace{\xi E\eta(2-L_{1}\eta)-\varOmega_{1}-\varOmega_{2}}_{T_{2}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.8.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="A2.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varOmega_{1}=2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varOmega_{1}=2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}E\eta B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.9.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="A2.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varOmega_{2}=L_{1}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varOmega_{2}=L_{1}E\eta^{2}\sigma^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the optimal solution of objective <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{r=0}^{R-1}(\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}])=\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}_{1}+\mathcal{L}_{1}-\mathcal{L}_{2}+\cdots+\mathcal{L}_{R-1}-\mathcal{L}_{R}=\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}_{R}\leq\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{r=0}^{R-1}(\mathcal{L}_{rE}-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{(r+1)E}])=\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}_{1}+\mathcal{L}_{1}-\mathcal{L}_{2}+\cdots+\mathcal{L}_{R-1}-\mathcal{L}_{R}=\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}_{R}\leq\mathcal{L}_{0}-\mathcal{L}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the denominator of the above equation in Eq. <a href="#A2.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.3 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a> should satisfy <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
so we can easily obtain the following condition for <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&lt;\frac{2\xi-2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}B}{L_{1}(\xi+\sigma^{2})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&lt;\frac{2\xi-2(|\mathcal{C}|-1)L_{2}B}{L_{1}(\xi+\sigma^{2})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Non-convex convergence rate of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> provides convergence rate of <span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>, which can confine the gradients of the objective function <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> to any bound, denoted as <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, after carefully selecting the number of rounds <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#A2.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.3 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a> and hyperparameters <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#A2.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ B.3.3 Completing the Proof of Theorem ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>. The smaller <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is, the larger <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is, which means that the tighter the bound is, the more communication rounds <math id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is required. We have completed the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Non-convex convergence rate of FedDifRC). ‣ B.3 Completing Proofs ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis for FedDifRC ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for <span id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experimental Details and Extra Results</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we additionally provide more experimental results. All experiments are conducted on a 64-bit Ubuntu-18.04 system with two NVIDIA RTX A5000 GPUs. Note that all results reported are the average of three repeating runs with a standard deviation of different random seeds.</p>
</div>
