<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 10</span>: </span><span id="A3.T10.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison results on CIFAR10-LT, CIFAR100-LT, and TinyImageNet-LT datasets with imbalance shift, <math id="A3.T10.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> means the long-tailed ratio between sample sizes of the most frequent and least frequent class (<span id="A3.T10.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="A3.T10.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\max_{j}\{n_{j}\}/\min_{j}\{n_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\max_{j}\{n_{j}\}/\min_{j}\{n_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Experimental Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all experiments, we run <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=100</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and set the number of clients as <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=10</annotation></semantics></math>. We conduct local training for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=10</annotation></semantics></math> epochs in each communication round using the SGD optimizer with a learning rate of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, a momentum of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, a batch size of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math>, and a weight decay set <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-5</annotation></semantics></math>.
We apply the data augmentation of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> in TinyImageNet dataset experiments.
The regularization coefficient of FedProx <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned across <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{10^{-4},10^{-3},10^{-2},10^{-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{10^{-4},10^{-3},10^{-2},10^{-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and is selected to be <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>;
the regularization coefficient of MOON <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned across <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.1,1.0,3.0,5.0,6.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.1,1.0,3.0,5.0,6.0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and is selected to be <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>;
the regularization coefficient of FedProto <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite> <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned across <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1.0,2.0,3.0,4.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1.0,2.0,3.0,4.0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and is selected to be <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>;
the smoothing parameter of FedNH <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">72</a>]</cite> <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned across <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.1,0.2,0.5,0.7,0.8,0.9\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.1,0.2,0.5,0.7,0.8,0.9\}</annotation></semantics></math> and is selected to be <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>;
the regularization coefficient of FedRCL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned across <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.2,0.4,0.6,0.8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.2,0.4,0.6,0.8\}</annotation></semantics></math> and is selected to be <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.6</annotation></semantics></math>, and divergence penalty <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned across <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.5,1.0,2.0,3.0,4.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.5,1.0,2.0,3.0,4.0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and is selected to be <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>;
the temperature parameter of FedLID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned across <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.02,0.04,0.06,0.08,0.1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.04</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.06</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.08</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.02,0.04,0.06,0.08,0.1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and is selected to be <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}=0.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}=0.04</annotation></semantics></math>.
We take out a 20% subset of the training set for validation and return the validation set back to the training set, and retrain the model after selecting the optimal hyperparameters <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.06</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.06</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=150</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
