</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.3 </span>Comparison results with domain shift</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The comparison results of Digits and Office-Caltech with domain shift are shown in Table. <a href="#A3.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ C.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details and Extra Results ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, where different clients are equipped with the data samples from different domains: Digits (MNIST: 1, USPS: 4, SVHN: 3, SYN: 2) and Office-Caltech (Caltech: 3, Webcam: 2, Amazon: 2, DSLR: 3). Each client’s dataset is randomly selected from the domains (Digits: 10%, Office-Caltech: 20%). The experiments show that <span id="A3.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> performs significantly better than other FL baselines, which confirms that our proposed <span id="A3.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> can acquire well-generalizable property of the feature space during the heterogeneous FL training with domain shift.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2507.06482v1/fig_app2.png" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:672/206;" width="672" height="206" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A3.F8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The t-SNE visualization of <span id="A3.F8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> on local clients under the CIFAR10 dataset (<math id="A3.F8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><mn>0.2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=10</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2507.06482v1/fig_app3.png" id="A3.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/275;" width="685" height="275" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A3.F9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The t-SNE visualization of <span id="A3.F9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> and FedAvg on the global model under the CIFAR10 dataset (<math id="A3.F9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><mn>0.2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=10</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.4 </span>Comparison results of convergence rates</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The comparison results of convergence rates on CIFAR10, CIFAR100, and TinyImageNet are shown in Table <a href="#A3.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ C.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details and Extra Results ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. Our <span id="A3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> required fewer rounds to converge compared with other baselines and achieved a higher final accuracy, showing the superiority of <span id="A3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> in dealing with <span id="A3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">non-iid</span> data and its robust stability, which also indicates that <span id="A3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> helps to promote training generalizability and efficiency of heterogeneous FL in the feature space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.5 </span>Effects of time-steps <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and temperature <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To explore the influence of time-steps <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <span id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">9</span> and temperature <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <span id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">11</span>, we conduct experiments on CIFAR10 with <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><mn>0.2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}</annotation></semantics></math>, shown in Fig. <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.2.2 Comparison results with imbalance shift ‣ C.2 Extra Results ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details and Extra Results ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. In Fig. <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.2.2 Comparison results with imbalance shift ‣ C.2 Extra Results ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details and Extra Results ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> left, we add different amounts of noise to get <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <span id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">9</span>, <span id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> is robust to the choice of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[100,300]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>100,300</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[100,300]</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=150</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the highest value). With the increase of time-steps <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, more and more details are removed and semantic-level features are preserved, but when <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is too large, the object structure is distorted in the sample, making poor performance. In Fig. <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.2.2 Comparison results with imbalance shift ‣ C.2 Extra Results ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details and Extra Results ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> right, we show the results with different <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <span id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">11</span>, which reveals that <span id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FedDifRC</span> is not sensitive to the <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[0.04,0.08]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.04</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[0.04,0.08]</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating the effectiveness of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <span id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">10</span>, to balance relative distances among different samples. The accuracy no longer increases after <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.06</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.06</annotation></semantics></math>. In Table. <a href="#A3.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ C.2.2 Comparison results with imbalance shift ‣ C.2 Extra Results ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details and Extra Results ‣ FedDifRC: Unlocking the Potential of Text-to-Image Diffusion Models in Heterogeneous Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, we provide results of the time-steps <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> for different datasets with <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙽𝙸𝙳𝟷</mi><mn>0.2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{NID1}_{0.2}</annotation></semantics></math> setting. Based on these results, to prevent the redundancy of adjusting parameters, we thus set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=150</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.06</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.06</annotation></semantics></math> in our experiments as default values.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T14" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.T14.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:496.9pt;height:113.9pt;vertical-align:-53.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(87.9pt,-20.2pt) scale(1.54777233856193,1.54777233856193) ;">
<table id="A3.T14.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T14.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F8F8F9;">
